    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>’s last imperial dynasty, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Gia Long</a> in 1802 after he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tay Son</a> and united the country.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minh-mang">Minh Mang</a> built a centralised Confucian state on the Qing model, renamed the country Dai Nam and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>.</li><li>French conquest from 1858 reduced the emperors to figureheads, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> abdicated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> in 1945.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The name Viet Nam was granted by the Qing emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaqing-emperor">Jiaqing</a> in 1804, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Gia Long</a> asked for Nam Viet, which recalled the ancient kingdom of Nanyue in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

